    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0545" n="477" xml:id="pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857/30½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">10 September, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The only present comment
                    necessary on these letters,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d428-f1"/> obviously meant to
                    be reassuring, is that my original error in speaking of “unarmed” vessels when I
                    should have said “unresisting” is now rising up to embarrass us, for which I am
                    very sorry.</p>
                <p>The reply about the <hi rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi>, if correctly outlined in
                    the newspapers this morning, is not very promising of a fulfilment of what
                    Bernstorff indicates as the attitude of his government in these letters.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
